Name: Linux filesystem root
Id: linux-root
Priority: 30          # probed after the Windows layouts; its markers cannot collide with theirs
Provisional: false
Platform: linux             # modules for the other platform are left out of the plan for this target
Description: >
  A Linux filesystem root, or the part of one that was collected. Covers a tar of /etc and
  /var/log and files exported from X-Ways or FTK, which land as an ordinary folder on Windows,
  and a UAC collection, whose [root] becomes this root when the archive is extracted.
Notes: >
  MatchMode is 'any' deliberately. A partial export is the normal case rather than the exception:
  an analyst who pulls only /var/log should still get the log modules, with everything needing
  /etc skipping with a reason. Requiring all markers would reject exactly the collections this
  layout exists to handle.

  The markers are chosen to be impossible on a Windows collection, so priority ordering against
  the Windows layouts never matters.
Detect:
  RootIsSelection: true
  Markers:
    - 'etc/passwd'
    - 'etc/os-release'
    - 'var/log'
  MatchMode: any
Resolve:
  RootOffset: '.'
  Unescape: none
  # root is a profile in its own right, not a directory containing profiles, which is why this
  # is a list rather than a single parent.
  UserProfiles:
    - 'home/*'
    - 'root'
